{"_id":"eqtp000000000001","name":"ADVENTURER (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"adventurer_L","tier":"L","months":24,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":"1d10!open"},"statGains":{"raw":"choice of two different stats","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"choice of two different stats"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>This is the character who seeks his fame and fortune by exploration and taking risks with his own life. The adventurer is at home in most types of habited places as well as many kinds of wilderness locales.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000002","name":"ADVISOR (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"advisor_L","tier":"L","months":97,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":"1d10!open"},"statGains":{"raw":"Intuition","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Intuition"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>Great rulers need great advice. The Advisor is in a position of authority and respect, but he still must please his lord to maintain his position. Advisors are masters of wisdom, influence, and intrigue. Advisors tend to find themselves in many situations of temptation. Some succumb to baser desires, but every so often a man of true virtue is able to maintain his authority and loyalty to his liege.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000003","name":"AGENT (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"agent_V","tier":"V","months":44,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"","type":"none","note":""},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>This is a vocation that encompasses parts of the FBI , Secret Service, and similar agencies that use mostly investigative agents instead of undercover or combat operations. Agent training denotes a direct working style, meaning they operate and interact with citizens on an “honest” level.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000004","name":"AMATEUR MAGE (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"amateur_mage_L","tier":"L","months":53,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"one realm stat, Memory","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"one realm stat, Memory"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The Amateur Mage studies magic in his off-time. He is intrigued by the powers of magic and wants to know more.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000005","name":"ANIMAL FRIEND (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"animal_friend_L","tier":"L","months":102,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"Empathy","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Empathy"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>Generally a loner, except for his animal friends, this type of character spends a great deal of time in the wilderness.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000006","name":"ANIMAL HANDLER (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"animal_handler_V","tier":"V","months":37,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"Animal Friend Training Package or 90+ temporary Empathy statistic [-2 points]","type":"none","note":"Animal Friend Training Package or 90+ temporary Empathy statistic [-2 points]"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The animal handler is often employed by spell users of the Corpist school of magic. An animal handler is skilled at keeping, grooming, raising, breeding, and healing a wide variety of animals or creatures. Animal handlers may make profits with trained animal acts, zoos, or by stocking catalyst sources, though some do keep animals as a hobby.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000007","name":"ANTAGONIST (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"antagonist_L","tier":"L","months":75,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>Antagonists try to expose flaws in plans, point out the obvious, and generally make a nuisance of themselves. The best Antagonists manage to do this so subtly that other characters don’t even realize that their efforts have been sabotaged by their own companion.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000008","name":"APOTHECARY (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"apothecary_V","tier":"V","months":27,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>Seeing the efficacy of herbal medicines, Apothecaries attempt to distill the essence of the herbs into more potent elixers and philters. While the success of Apothecaries in the arts of medicine and healing may be at question, their skill with poisons is undisputed</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000009","name":"ARACHNAMANCER (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"arachnamancer_L","tier":"L","months":164,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"None","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"None"},"qualifier":{"raw":"None","type":"none","note":"None"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The arachnamancer is an unusual essence user who has developed a great affinity for spiders. By studying the lifestyle and manners of many different types of spiders, the arachnamancer has developed a unique list that allows him to mimic many of the powers of the spider. It is theorized that intensive study of other animal group scould yield similar results, though no such research has ever been completed or developed to the extent of the arachnamancer.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000010","name":"ARCHITECT (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"architect_V","tier":"V","months":19,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":"1d10!open"},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The Architect is hired to build sturdy towers, castles, and keeps. Architects design and organize the building of all of their structures, normally without the aid of any drafting. Castles can be built without an architect, but when siege engines begin to close in, it’s nice to know that the walls were built by the best.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000011","name":"ARCHAEOLOGIST (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"archaeologist_V","tier":"V","months":52,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>So much of the past has been forgotten that some individuals make it their job to return lost lore and items to civilization. Archaeologists are academic in nature, but adventurous at heart. Clearing monsters from a ruin is only the first step in the Archaeologist’s adventure into the past.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000012","name":"ARMS INSTRUCTOR (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"arms_instructor_L","tier":"L","months":106,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"A total of 10 ranks in skills from any of the following groups: Combat Maneuvers or Weapon Group. [-3 points]","type":"none","note":"A total of 10 ranks in skills from any of the following groups: Combat Maneuvers or Weapon Group. [-3 points]"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The arms instructor is a character who makes his living by teaching his skill at arms to wealthy students. Successful arms instructors need not only skill in combat, but also skill in diplomacy in order to keep their students corning back for more training.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000013","name":"ARTIFICER (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"artificer_L","tier":"L","months":110,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The Artificer is fascinated by the toys of magic. Whenever possible the Artificer will pick up new magic items for use or even just curiousity. This fascination and greater understanding of magic items provides the Artificer with greater ability to access and use magic items.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000014","name":"ARTIST (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"artist_V","tier":"V","months":28,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":"1d10!open"},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The artist has made a life of crafting pieces of artwork. Most artists have a patron who provides them with a place to live and the means to live in return for the creations they produce.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000015","name":"ARTIST (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"artist_L","tier":"L","months":89,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"Empathy and Intuition","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Empathy and Intuition"},"qualifier":{"raw":"one skill in the Artistic group at two ranks","type":"none","note":"one skill in the Artistic group at two ranks"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>An artist uses some form of alternate communication to express emotions or ideas to others. This person can use almost any form of art, painting, sculpture, light shows, huge umbrellas, or music as their medium. People may or may not like what the artist is doing giving the artist a license to be erratic or eccentric, socially and mentally.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000016","name":"ASSASSIN (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"assassin_V","tier":"V","months":30,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":"1d10!open"},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>A professional, hired by someone to kill someone else. This occupation is perhaps one of the most dangerous. However, it is possible that an assassin can be owed favors by one or more people in high ranking positions in society (denoted by “High ranking favor” below).</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000017","name":"ASTRONOMER (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"astronomer_L","tier":"L","months":78,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The Astronomer studies the stellar, lunar, and solar cycles and links their passage to daily occurrences. An Astronomer is not content just to study and predict these cycles. A true Astronomer seeks to know why the cycles work the way they do. They strive to learn the secrets of heaven so that they can understand the earth. The Astronomer’s constant study and focus tend to make him self-absorbed or too technical minded for easy conversation with non-Astronomers.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000018","name":"ATHLETE (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"athlete_L","tier":"L","months":61,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"Constitution, Self-Discipline and choice of either Quickness or Strength","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Constitution, Self-Discipline and choice of either Quickness or Strength"},"qualifier":{"raw":"one skill in the Artistic group at two ranks","type":"none","note":"one skill in the Artistic group at two ranks"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>Athletes are devoted to the pursuit of excellence in physical prowess. This can be in any physical game or challenge. An athlete will be able to overcome the potentially arduous physical rigors of operations without much difficulty.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000019","name":"BEASTMASTER (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"beastmaster_L","tier":"L","months":124,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"Empathy","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Empathy"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>A natural affinity with animals enables the Beastmaster to befriend creatures of the wilds. This friendship is deepened by magic to an almost symbiotic relationship, where each partner pledges loyalty and assistance to the other. Beastmasters will sometimes be ill at ease in the company of members of their own race, preferring the honesty of their animal companions.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000020","name":"BERSERKER (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"berserker_L","tier":"L","months":64,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"Strength","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Strength"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>A berserker is trained to lose control of his normal sensibilities in battle and become a fierce killing machine.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000021","name":"BODYGUARD (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"bodyguard_V","tier":"V","months":30,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"None","type":"none","note":"None"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The bodyguard specializes in protecting the life of a patron from attackers. The bodyguard learns how to anticipate and counter attacks as well as advising his client on the best course for his own personal safely.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000022","name":"BURGLAR (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"burglar_V","tier":"V","months":33,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>A burglar makes his living stealing goods from peoples homes or businesses. They ply their trade around heavily populated areas and then move on to another area.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000023","name":"CARAVAN GUARD (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"caravan_guard_V","tier":"V","months":null,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"None","type":"none","note":"None"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The caravan guard is a character who escorts merchant caravans from city to city and protects them from bandit attacks. The caravan guard learns in be a shrewd judge of character, as well as a fierce combatant. Because the caravan guard is frequently outnumbered by less-experienced foes, he has learned to use strike quickly and decisively to protect himself. In the course of his journeys, a caravan guard will encounter many different cultures and customs.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000024","name":"CATALYST COLLECTOR (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"catalyst_collector_V","tier":"V","months":37,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"None","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"None"},"qualifier":{"raw":"None","type":"none","note":"None"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>Catalyst collectors make a living by supplying the various magic catalysts to the magic practitioners. Catalyst collectors are adventurers who seek out the rarer and more dangerous catalysts for profit. While they mayor may not have any ability to cast magic, they are aware of the principles of magic and spell casting. Catalyst collectors often find employment working for guilds and colleges, where large amounts of simple catalysts are expended by students and the more rare are used by the masters.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000025","name":"CHANCELLOR (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"chancellor_V","tier":"V","months":64,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"At least 12 ranks in Religion [-4 points]","type":"none","note":"At least 12 ranks in Religion [-4 points]"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>A Chancellor handles the administrative affairs of a religion. He is also a spiritual leader of a congregation of believers. The Chancellor's job is to provide support and inspiration to the followers of his religion. He also handles and presides over many of the religion's ceremonies. Bringing the actual teaching to ministers, a Chancellor handles the major decisions that a religion has to face.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000026","name":"CHAPLAIN (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"chaplain_V","tier":"V","months":43,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":"1d10!open"},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>A lord generally selects a clergy member to preside over the lord’s religious services. A Chaplain is the lord’s spiritual advisor and thereby a spiritual leader of the lord’s land. Chaplains often head up the education of the lord’s children as the clergy is often the only literate class. A GM may decide that all clergy members who preside over a church may also choose this training package.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000027","name":"CHARLATAN (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"charlatan_L","tier":"L","months":102,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":"1d10!open"},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>Misdirection, authentic-seeming tomes, mystical implements, and a glib tongue are the Charlatan's best tools in prising gold from the gullible and the greedy. To one patron, the Charlatan may claim to have uncovered the secrets of transmutation, to another the formula for eternal youth, but to both he will explain his need for monies in order to acquire the exotic ingredients and perform the necessary experiments... And once his prey is adequately fleeced, he will flee before his chicanery is discovered. Some few have added scraps of magic to their repertoire of deception, enhancing both trickery and credibility as well as masking their true intent from real masters of magic.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000028","name":"CHI MASTER (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"chi_master_L","tier":"L","months":null,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"Self Discipline","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Self Discipline"},"qualifier":{"raw":"A total of 10 skill ranks in the Self Control skill category. [-3 points]","type":"none","note":"A total of 10 skill ranks in the Self Control skill category. [-3 points]"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The Chi Master has dedicated himself to leaning how to focus the energy of his mind and body to perform supernatural feats. The years of dedication and training required to reach the levels of mastery and control necessary have imbued the him with a strong will and tireless energy.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000029","name":"CITY GUARD (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"city_guard_V","tier":"V","months":25,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>Almost every urban area has some sort of paid police force. These character are in charge of making sure that the city remains free of bedlam in the streets. If a promotion is gained (in the Special section), the character has been promoted in the ranks (more promotions equate to higher ranks).</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000030","name":"CIVIL SERVANT (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"civil_servant_V","tier":"V","months":21,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":"1d10!open"},"statGains":{"raw":"","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":""},"qualifier":{"raw":"","type":"none","note":""},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>Civil Servants are paid public officials. In this respect, they are similar to City Guards . However, their duties are usually very bureaucratic in nature.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000031","name":"CLEANER (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"cleaner_L","tier":"L","months":92,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"Self-Discipline and Strength","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Self-Discipline and Strength"},"qualifier":{"raw":"at least a +5 total Self-Discipline bonus and a total Empathy bonus no greater than +0","type":"none","note":"at least a +5 total Self-Discipline bonus and a total Empathy bonus no greater than +0"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>This is an individual who “cleans up” botched operations by eliminating all traces of the operation, including, sometimes, the agents themselves. Cleaners are also used on insanely risky operations, not because they are suicidal, but because they will do “anything” to complete an operation.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000032","name":"CLERGY (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"clergy_L","tier":"L","months":null,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"Memory","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Memory"},"qualifier":{"raw":"1 skill in the Influence group at 2 ranks. [-3 points]","type":"none","note":"1 skill in the Influence group at 2 ranks. [-3 points]"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The life of a member of the clergy is an existence for only the most devout. These members of an organized religion usually have a strict code of ethics and behavior they must observe to maintain favor in their faith. On occasion, a member of the clergy will be sent out into the world to right wrongs and spread the faith.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000033","name":"CLOAKED VIGILANTE (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"cloaked_vigilante_L","tier":"L","months":161,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"2 skills in the Subterfuge group at 2 ranks each. 1 rank in a skill in the Urban group. [-4 points]","type":"none","note":"2 skills in the Subterfuge group at 2 ranks each. 1 rank in a skill in the Urban group. [-4 points]"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The Cloaked Vigilante is an individual who has lost faith in the proficiency of the local constabulary to enforce laws, usually against a criminal element, though sometimes it is those in lawful positions who are the wrong-doers. He therefore endeavors to “take the law into his own hands,” and launches his own, personal crusade, functioning outside the law, against injustice (or justice, or whatever other cause he might be campaigning against). He traditionally keeps his identity a secret, to protect his public life and those relations he may keep in it, for these would be obvious targets for the Vigilante’s enemies. Famous Cloaked Vigilantes might include The Shadow, The Phantom Detective, The Spider (Master of Men!), The Batman, The Phantom, The Green Hornet, The Avenger.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000034","name":"CLOISTERED ACADEMIC (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"cloistered_academic_L","tier":"L","months":95,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The cloistered academic spends his days locked away from the rest of the world, embroiled in his learning. Books are his life. If he is close to anyone, it will usually only be a small pet. Even servants and others living in the same household are largely ignored.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000035","name":"CLOISTERED ZEALOT (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"cloistered_zealot_L","tier":"L","months":128,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The Cloistered Zealot lives a life of purity and scholarship in the name of his deity. Cloistered Zealots find a solid balance between preaching their religion and addressing the realities of life. Cloistered Zealots are well respected for their insights, wisdom, and intelligence.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000036","name":"COMBAT MEDIC (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"combat_medic_V","tier":"V","months":35,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>A Combat Medic provides rudimentary medical service to small combat units on the front line or in areas too far away for relatively quick medical attention. These people are trained in field medicine, survival, and tactical skills. While they are medics and under the Hippocratic oath, they must sometimes choose whether to enter combat offensively as opposed to defensively.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000037","name":"CON MAN (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"con_man_V","tier":"V","months":32,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":"1d10!open"},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The lure of quick money often draws street urchins into the realm of the Con Man. The Con Man is adept at setting people up to rip them off. He often has several identities that he can assume (and proper papers to back up the identities).</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000038","name":"CONJUROR (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"conjuror_L","tier":"L","months":84,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"Memory","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Memory"},"qualifier":{"raw":"At least 2 ranks in Magical Ritual (Summoning) , and at least 4 ranks of skills in the Lore • Obscure skill category, and at least 4 ranks in any “summoning” spell list (see the list above).","type":"none","note":"At least 2 ranks in Magical Ritual (Summoning) , and at least 4 ranks of skills in the Lore • Obscure skill category, and at least 4 ranks in any “summoning” spell list (see the list above)."},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>Secluded from most of society with only their summoned and conjured companions as friends, the Conjurors venture out only with their thralls (much to the scorn of the local populace).</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000039","name":"CORPIST CASTER (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"corpist_caster_L","tier":"L","months":40,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"None","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"None"},"qualifier":{"raw":"None","type":"none","note":"None"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>Corpists are often considered macabre or evil. Corpists use the body parts ofcreatures in order to affect magic. The more magical the creature the better the catalyst, so Corpists are often quite eager to join with adventurers just for the opportunity to gather catalyst material. While Corpist casters can be quite likable in most respects, it is difficult to be used to the smell that often seems to follow them. Also, familiars (and their magicians) tend to be very wary of such casters.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000040","name":"COURT MAGICIAN (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"court_magician_L","tier":"L","months":97,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>Lords can be quite demanding when seeking to satisfy their entertainment needs. Sometimes a lord will keep a magician on staff for the sole purpose of entertaining and impressing him and his guests. A Court Magician learns to couple his magic talents with showmanship for a grand display of magic power. Court Magicians may also serve in advisory positions, but they are generally considered to be flamboyant performers and not well learned sages.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000041","name":"CRAFTER (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"crafter_V","tier":"V","months":28,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":"1d10!open"},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>Many people are good with their hands and have the desire to create things. This training package represents all those people; from the blacksmith, to the coppersmith, to the jeweler.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000042","name":"CRUSADING ACADEMIC (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"crusading_academic_L","tier":"L","months":110,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>Having spent years studying, the Crusading Academic now has a cause and is ready to tell the world about it. He is ready to travel the world, meet new people, and see strange places.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000043","name":"CRYSTALIST CASTER (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"crystalist_caster_L","tier":"L","months":46,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"None","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"None"},"qualifier":{"raw":"None","type":"none","note":"None"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>For Crystalists, power and wealth are synonymous: the most powerful Crystalists also carry the most elegant gems and stones. Crystalist can enchant gemstones to become the fuel and catalyst for their spells. Each casting erodes a part of this enchantment, so the crystals must be periodically re-enchanted. Crystalist do not have to spend as much time scrounging for catalysts as Herbalist or Corpists, but instead they must constantly spend their time re-enchanting their crystals. Crystalists tend to be flamboyant and extravagant, often wearing as many precious gems as they can afford all at the same time.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000044","name":"CULTIST (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"cultist_L","tier":"L","months":129,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":"1d10!open"},"statGains":{"raw":"Reasoning","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Reasoning"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>A cultist studies the ways of summoning and conjuring. They can be either the leader of a strange cult, a follower of such a cult, or a character with extensive knowledge of such cults sent to destroy them. In all cases, they are experts on finding signs of the supernatural and extra-planar, and how to deal with the creatures that are summoned from other planes.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000045","name":"CUT PURSE (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"cut_purse_V","tier":"V","months":37,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":"1d10!open"},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>A specialized type of thief, the Cut Purse works the streets. He is particularly adept at watching crowds and determining who should have the heaviest pockets.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000046","name":"DEMONOLOGIST (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"demonologist_L","tier":"L","months":132,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"None","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"None"},"qualifier":{"raw":"Dark Pact flaw, Open Door flaw, or Dark Temptation flaw [-7 points]","type":"none","note":"Dark Pact flaw, Open Door flaw, or Dark Temptation flaw [-7 points]"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>A demonologist specializes in dealing with demons. Demonologists are not always evil, though continued interchange with demons always leaves its mark, and all demonologists eventually succumb to the evil influences of the demons with which he interacts. Demonologists may have dealings with demons of the Pales, most often the demons of the Void have the knowledge and power with which to tempt the demonologist. Demons of the Pale are generally used for drudge work or simple tasks, while the demons of the Void are the source of infernal knowledge.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000047","name":"DETECTIVE (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"detective_V","tier":"V","months":33,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>A detective is the character who investigates a mysterious happening. This could be a member of the city guard or a specialist called upon when needed. A detective is rarely found outside an urban environment unless he is seeking clues to the current case.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000048","name":"DILETTANTE (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"dilettante_L","tier":"L","months":145,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"Presence","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Presence"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>Usually born to a noble, or rich family with a large silver spoon in his mouth, the Dilettante rarely cares about any one thing, save perhaps his personal freedom. The idle rich, he has always had the best of everything, and thus lacks many skills that make normal folks...well, normal. He is well-educated, having attended the best (usually Ivy-League) schools. Herein often lies the greatest irony; for the affairs of the Dilettante offer a most unusual “cover” for other, more shadowy practices. Many heroes are Dilettantes in their public (secret) identities, while wearing the mantle of the Cloaked Vigilante or Gangster to root out their foes. After all, who else would have the time or cash to traipse about everywhere seeking out enemies to thrash? The Dilettante, of course. Whether a facade masking criminal activities or crime-busting, who would suspect the spoiled rich have any interest in such matters? This cover leaves the Dilettante free to conduct his more important affairs in secret, free from the prying eyes of those who might attempt to hinder him. Famous names among the ranks of Dilettantism might include: Lamont Cranston, Bruce Wayne, Howard Hughes, Richard Wentworth, Richard Curtis Van Loan, and Alphonse Capone.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000049","name":"DIPLOMAT (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"diplomat_V","tier":"V","months":48,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":"1d10!open"},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>A diplomat is a person who has made it his job to negotiate and talk to various other people in positions of power and authority. He is usually well versed in more than one culture and has contacts in many cities.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000050","name":"DOCTOR (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"doctor_V","tier":"V","months":18,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>A doctor is a person dedicated to tended to the sick. This should include all types of persons who are caring for the sick, not just those that actually perform the healing (e.g., the nurses, attendants, etc.). Most people who tend to the sick are doing so on a voluntary basis.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000051","name":"DREAM TRAVELLER (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"dream_traveller_L","tier":"L","months":122,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>To the uninitiated, sleep is merely relief from the troubles of the waking world, and bodily rest. To the Dream Traveller, sleep is the doorway into the dream world, a world as dangerous as the mundane world, with its own inexplicable physical laws and mind-bending unreality. Of all the mortal wayfarers in the dream realm, the Dream Traveller is most able to explore in safety, by using magic to strengthen the dream-self with the abilities of the other world; others are unprotected against the anarchy of dreams.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000052","name":"DREAMWEAVER (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"dreamweaver_L","tier":"L","months":124,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The Dreamweaver has specialized in tapping the power of the mind through dreams, being able to select and manipulate dreams, whether for divination, wish fulfilment, or to increase creativity. He also possesses almost total control of his sleeping pattern. With preparation, he can influence the dreams of others, inducing daydreams of pleasant aspect or nightmares ofhellish terror as he chooses.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000053","name":"DUELIST (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"duelist_V","tier":"V","months":32,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>Where words leave off, swords pick up. Often disputes are settled in duels of honor. A duelist is a professional settler of such disputes. They can be hired to fight for lords, so the lord need not worry about his own safety. A duelist is adept at single combat, but not neccesarily honorable combat. A duelist fights with honor only so long as he is sure he can win.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000054","name":"ENGINEER (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"engineer_L","tier":"L","months":85,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":"1d10!open"},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>Great castles require great architects, while enchanted castles require enchanted architects. The Engineer not only knows how to design, build, and organize a construction project, but also how to enchant it. In worlds where the magic flies fast and furious, no home is truly sound unless it is built by an experienced Engineer.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000055","name":"ENTERTAINER (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"entertainer_V","tier":"V","months":53,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>Between movies, books, music, and television, the entertainment industry virtually had its birth during the Pulp era. Entertainment provided an escape from the horrors of the Great Depression, at least for a little while. With the increased popularity in movies, a new breed of celebrity appeared: the movie star. With spotlights, gala premieres, awards ceremonies, and glamorous life styles, movie stars embodied all that Americans wished their lives were. Some famous entertainers include Errol Flynn, Clark Gable, Olivia DeHavilland, Cary Grant, Jimmy Stewart, Kenneth Robeson (actually Lester Dent, author of Doc Savage), and George Burns.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000056","name":"ENTREPRENEUR (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"entrepreneur_V","tier":"V","months":85,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The Entrepreneur begins his career as a white-collar worker, in an office, working the standard (as of 1938) 40-hour work week. He enters into commercial enterprises on a regular basis, taking risks, endeavoring to rise through the ranks of the business world. Wealth, power and social position are the Entrepreneur’s motivating factors, (much as they are to the Dilettante) and he works hard to get ahead (unlike the Dilettante ). Famous Entrepreneurs might include: J.D. Rockefeller, Howard Hughes, or Bruce Wayne.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000057","name":"EXECUTIONER (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"executioner_V","tier":"V","months":28,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>Even the most benevolent of rulers find that they must sometimes punish criminals, spies, or enemies with painful death. The Executioner is trained to do so with great efficiency. Executioners are trained in the art of torture and interrogation as well. In lands with public beheadings or hangings, the Executioner is often expected to make a grand display of torturing the prisoner for as long as possible. An Executioner with a brutal reputation can be a deterrent to criminals and spies by mere rumor alone.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000058","name":"EXPLORER (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"explorer_L","tier":"L","months":66,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"Constitution, choice of one other stat","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Constitution, choice of one other stat"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>Similar to the Adventurer, the Explorer specializes in travelling in uncharted areas and outdoor exploration. This could include sailing explorers as well as overland explorers.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000059","name":"FEMME FATALE (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"femme_fatale_V","tier":"V","months":49,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"Female","type":"none","note":"Female"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The Femme Fatale is an exercise in seduction. She (a predominantly female vocation) uses those natural gifts to play upon her victim and his resources for her own gain. The seductress will usually present herself as sympathetic to one’s plight until she has attained her goal, then will turn on her “benefactor” and betray him in some fashion, even if it is just abandonment. The Femme Fatale has little sense of morality, and will go to great lengths to accomplish her task. It is not to say she will positively attempt to hurt her victim, whether physically or emotionally, but that she is simply out for herself. If she should desire to continue the relationship, then that becomes one of the goals she will attempt to attain. Many Pulps stereotyped the role as that belonging to an Oriental enchantress, with name-tags like: The Dragon Lady, Serpent Lady, Empress of the East, etc. Infamous Femme Fatales might include: Mata Hari, Thelda Blanchet, Elsa Schneider, Princess Aura, Princess Kojii, and Ayesha-She Who Must Be Obeyed.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000060","name":"FIELD SCIENTIST (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"field_scientist_V","tier":"V","months":30,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>A cross between a lab scientists and an academic, members of this vocation pursue hands-on research outside of the lab. Trained to operate in adverse or unusual surroundings and circumstances, this vocation can include Archaeologists, Anthropologists, Ecologists and Researchers.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000061","name":"FORTUNE TELLER (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"fortune_teller_V","tier":"V","months":40,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>Often self-taught, some Fortune tellers earn their living from reassuring the anxious about the future, to others it is a pastime with which to entertain their jaded friends. Success in prediction is as much due to an eloquent flow of words and understanding the querent as to any true ability.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000062","name":"GADGETEER (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"gadgeteer_V","tier":"V","months":44,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The gadgeteer is an inventor with the ability to create machines that leap over current scientific restrictions. The gadgeteer can invent items that most only dream of and these inventions usually work correctly the first time. Of course, accidents do happen (usually destroying the only working prototype) but the gadgeteer continues undaunted.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000063","name":"GANGSTER (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"gangster_V","tier":"V","months":42,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>For the first part of the 1920s public opinion of the Gangster was positive, and the FBI’s “Ten Most Wanted” list made anti-heroes of its inductees. Legendary Gangsters became household names, and the public often followed their exploits in the papers and on the radio. Toward the end of the decade the popularity of the Gangster waned and the public threw its support with the G-Men, as more and more hapless citizens were caught in the crossfire between gangs. Gangs were frequently based on the extended family, with the Italian Mafia, Irish toughs, Oriental criminal societies such as the Tongs and Yakuza, and good ol’ American street punks often fighting each other for superiority. Famous Gangsters might include: Al Capone, John Dillenger, Bonnie & Clyde, “Dutch” Schultz, “Lucky” Luciano, “Bugs” Moran.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000064","name":"GRAVE ROBBER (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"grave_robber_V","tier":"V","months":45,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>Not everyone seeking the lost are as altruistic, or informed, as the Archaeologist . Many people are aware of jewelry being buried with a loved one, but the Grave Robber capitalizes on this information. A Grave Robber may seek out ancient grave sites, or even ruins, for their chance at quick and easy money. Of course, most people frown on such activities, and sometimes the dead themselves will rise up to protect their treasure, so though the money maybe quick, it isn’t always easy.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000065","name":"GREAT WHITE HUNTER (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"great_white_hunter_L","tier":"L","months":184,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"Constitution","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Constitution"},"qualifier":{"raw":"At least 2 skills in the Outdoor category at 2 ranks each. [-3 points]","type":"none","note":"At least 2 skills in the Outdoor category at 2 ranks each. [-3 points]"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>Great White Hunters (a stereotypical descriptive; not all were white, nor even great) are sometimes arrogant of their abilities, and sometimes need to be taken down a notch or two. They often lead hunting parties and caravans into the wilds of unexplored lands, just for the sake of the adventure. Famous Great White Hunters might include Allan Quatermain, Teddy “Rough Rider” Roosevelt, Charles Remington, “Buffalo Bill” Cody, and “Wild Bill” Hickok.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000066","name":"GROOM (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"groom_V","tier":"V","months":44,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>A Groom maintains and oversees a stable. A Groom may care solely for the lord’s horses or he may watch over any manner of creature for his lord, including pigeons, falcons, bees, and fantasy creatures. Grooms may garner friendship and respect from knights and nobility, as they maintain the horses that makes knights so devastating.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000067","name":"GUARDIAN (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"guardian_L","tier":"L","months":116,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"Constitution","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Constitution"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>A guardian is a person who is given a specific area or region to guard and protect. Sometimes, guardians work together in larger organizations to protect very large regions.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000068","name":"GUILD APPRENTICE (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"guild_apprentice_L","tier":"L","months":86,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"Memory and realm stat","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Memory and realm stat"},"qualifier":{"raw":"Total temporary stats for Memory and Reasoning of 180 or greater [-5 points]","type":"none","note":"Total temporary stats for Memory and Reasoning of 180 or greater [-5 points]"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>A guild apprentice is taught the lessons of magic by either a mercantile group of magicians or by a member of an established guild. Guild apprentices spend a lot of time studying magic in great detail, from books and from direct instruction from one or more masters. Guild apprentices tend to be well educated and prepared for a career in a city. Guild apprentices are generally taught magic that will assist their master in the day to day maintenance of a business as well as spells that assist them in their studies.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000069","name":"HEDGE WIZARD (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"hedge_wizard_L","tier":"L","months":30,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"None","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"None"},"qualifier":{"raw":"Magic Bane flaw [-7 points]","type":"none","note":"Magic Bane flaw [-7 points]"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>A hedge wizard is a primitive Essence user who has learned the trade through oral tradition and practice, not through studying dusty books. Hedge wizards are generally found in less civilized areas, though hedge wizards can thrive anywhere a grandparent teaches the old traditions to their relatives. A hedge wizard generally excels at ritual magic, while finding spell lists more difficult to learn. Since hedge wizards tend to require time to cast most of their magic. They are practiced at intimidating others, convincing them that while it may take the hedge wizard longer to cast a spell, it will be suitably nasty. Hedge wizards are sometimes confused with witches, warlocks, and shamans.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000070","name":"HERBALIST (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"herbalist_V","tier":"V","months":33,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":"1d10!open"},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>A herbalist is a person who specializes in growing, preparing, and cultivating herbs. Very often, herbalists are found near urban areas (where demand for herbs is higher), though they also like to secluded nature of a more rural environment.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000071","name":"HERBALIST CASTER (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"herbalist_caster_L","tier":"L","months":56,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"None","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"None"},"qualifier":{"raw":"None","type":"none","note":"None"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>Herbalists specialize in the understanding of plant life from an analytical point of view. Herbalists perceive plants as a natural source of power. An Herbalist differs from an animist in that an Herbalist perceives properties in the plant life, but does not worship plants. The Herbalist is analogous to a botanical chemist in some respects.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000072","name":"HERMIT (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"hermit_L","tier":"L","months":130,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"Self Discipline, Constitution","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Self Discipline, Constitution"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>Retreating from civilization, the Hermit leads a solitary life of unremitting hardship. He makes his abode in the wastes, whether it be in the frozen mountains, under the blazing desert sun or on bleak island haunts. Distanced from the distractions of mundane life, the Hermit searches for spiritual or philosophical enlightenment.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000073","name":"HIGHWAYMAN (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"highwayman_V","tier":"V","months":35,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":"1d10!open"},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>A highwayman is a roguish character who specializes in waylaying travellers on the road. They are often well-versed in regional lore and the outdoors in general.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000074","name":"HOURI (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"houri_L","tier":"L","months":108,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"Presence","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Presence"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>Sometimes courtesan, sometimes mistress, the Houri is the foremost practitioner of seduction and a skilled manipulator of all, but most especially members of the opposite sex. With sorcerous arts, the Houri can beguile even the most cold hearted, enhancing innate beauty and adopting the appearance of others, yet the rose is not without its thorn, for the kiss of a Houri can undo even the mighty.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000075","name":"HUNTER (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"hunter_L","tier":"L","months":18,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":"1d10!open"},"statGains":{"raw":"Constitution","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Constitution"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The Hunter is at home in the wilds. He ventures into the civilized areas only to buy supplies and sell his pelts.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000076","name":"INQUISITOR (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"inquisitor_V","tier":"V","months":55,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The inquisitor has a focused mission; discover any who are not believers in his faith. His reasons for doing this will differ from religion to religion. He might be simply checking up on the church in a particular region, sent to straighten things out, or he can be sent to root out and torture those who do not believe.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000077","name":"INSIDIOUS VILLAIN (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"insidious_villain_L","tier":"L","months":124,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"Presence","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Presence"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The Insidious Villain is the criminal mastermind. The master schemer, he always hatches some sort of diabolical plan to attain his desires, many times at any cost. He feels himself above the law, and unlike most “ordinary” criminals, fears no lawful repercussions for his actions. The Insidious Villain will go to any length to achieve his goals, whether it be planning a small heist or contriving to rule the world. Morality is not in his vocabulary, and he will always possess a nefarious master plan, some dastardly dark design that lurks in the recesses of his criminal mind, patiently awaiting fruition. Whatever his current activities, it can be a sure bet that it will lead to that grand scheme. Insidious Villains are known for their secret hideouts, which are of course filled with countless deathtraps, yet also contain the spoils of their wicked plots. Infamous Insidious Villains might include: Dr. Fu Manchu, Professor Moriarty, Ming the Merciless, John Sunlight, Mo-gwei, Shiwan Khan, Kathulos, Adolf Hitler, The Nine, Itsu-The Hand Sinister, and Mola Ram.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000078","name":"INTELLIGENCE ANALYST (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"intelligence_analyst_V","tier":"V","months":47,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>This is a job in which a person researches a particular area, social structure, or aspect of a given country (e.g., economics, crime, terrorism, etc.). These are usually not field operatives, but their knowledge is very valuable and in-depth in their areas of expertise to operatives in those areas. Analysts have been known to leave their cubicles once in a while on an operation, but it is usually in a consolatory capacity. If this person does make it in the field their knowledge could prove essential to a mission.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000079","name":"INVENTOR (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"inventor_V","tier":"V","months":45,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>New machines, siege engines, and mills do not just evolve, they are created. Inventors are considered unusual because they concentrate on mechanical and scientific problems to the exclusion of everyday affairs. Inventors are generally gifted in several crafts and arts.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000080","name":"JESTER (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"jester_V","tier":"V","months":52,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>Great rulers need great advice, but they also need to laugh. A Jester is a source of entertainment, advice, and diplomatic face-saving. The fool is sometimes abused, but most often they are well rewarded in food, clothing, and position. Even so, a lord or lady can always vent their ire or frustration on the affable fool instead of lashing out at powerful vassals.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000081","name":"JOURNALIST (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"journalist_V","tier":"V","months":27,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>Whether it’s a world-wide broadcast or local coverage of a community meeting, a Journalist strives to report the events objectively (although that doesn’t always happen). A Journalist will travel to where the action is, covertly if need be, to get the story before anyone else. Journalists can usually make good contacts in underworld areas and foreign governments during their search for the truth.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000082","name":"JOURNEYING APPRENTICE (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"journeying_apprentice_L","tier":"L","months":104,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"None","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"None"},"qualifier":{"raw":"None","type":"none","note":"None"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>A journeying apprentice learns from a master who rarely stays in one place. Journeying apprentices learn practical magic and practical skills that assist himself and his master on their journeys. Journeying apprentices often have less book learning than a guild apprentice, though they are used to harsh conditions and difficult situations. The journeying apprentice learns from his master while driving wagons, riding horses, sitting at roadside inns, or walking along country lanes. Wanderlust and a thirst for adventure draw these students to such a wayward lifestyle, while skill and wits are what keep them alive long enough to one day become masters themselves.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000083","name":"KNIGHT (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"knight_L","tier":"L","months":69,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"Strength, Self Discipline","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Strength, Self Discipline"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>A knight is a warrior dedicated to a cause or a lord (as opposed to a Paladin , who is dedicated to a greater power). A knight is known for his heavy armor and ability with weapons. Note that some GM’s may decide that the character who takes this package must also take the “Knighted” talent (see Appendix A-5 for more information on Talents).</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000084","name":"LABORER (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"laborer_V","tier":"V","months":14,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>Whenever raw manual labor is done, the people in charge rarely do it themselves. The nearby villages and towns were full of folks willing to work hard for a relatively small amount of money. Unskilled labor is often needed in and or around a castle (especially during construction of the structure).</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000085","name":"LAWYER (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"lawyer_L","tier":"L","months":117,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":"1d10!open"},"statGains":{"raw":"Memory and Presence","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Memory and Presence"},"qualifier":{"raw":"Acting at 2 ranks and any single skill in the Influence skill category at 2 ranks.","type":"none","note":"Acting at 2 ranks and any single skill in the Influence skill category at 2 ranks."},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>Not the first choice for a PC, but nonetheless an important character to have around when committing illegal acts. There will be times when an operation goes wrong and ends up being public; that’s when a Lawyer comes in handy. In such times a Lawyer is all that stands between you and judgement. In most U.S. law enforcement agencies, this is one of the predominant degrees/vocations for agents.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000086","name":"LIBRARIAN (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"librarian_V","tier":"V","months":57,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"None","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"None"},"qualifier":{"raw":"None","type":"none","note":"None"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The librarian may either be a serious book collector, or an organization freak for a collector or college, Librarians are fine researchers and great sources of information, though they are generally too sedentary to adventure abroad. The occasional librarian may go in search of a rare or exotic text, though they are often looked down on by the librarian elite. Librarians are also expected to act aloof and frown in dismay at the general ignorance of the populace whenever possible.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000087","name":"LOREMASTER (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"loremaster_V","tier":"V","months":40,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The perpetual scholar. The Loremaster studies, constantly striving to know all there is to know. Some Loremasters specialize in areas of knowledge; while others are diverse, knowing little bits about lots of things.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000088","name":"MAGIC CRAFTER (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"magic_crafter_L","tier":"L","months":72,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":"1d10!open"},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>Some simple craftsmen are not as simple as they seem. Some of the most impressive and sturdy crafts are made with a little magical assistance. Magic Crafters can be of any realm, and they gain access to the training package spell lists to help in their trade.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000089","name":"MANIPULATOR (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"manipulator_L","tier":"L","months":120,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"Presence","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Presence"},"qualifier":{"raw":"A total of at least 6 ranks of skills in the Influence skill category.","type":"none","note":"A total of at least 6 ranks of skills in the Influence skill category."},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>Behind the scenes, causing trouble, the Manipulator is rarely perceived as the source of the strife he creates. The extent of his influence is rarely ever known to anyone but himself.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000090","name":"MARINE PILOT (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"marine_pilot_V","tier":"V","months":39,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>Marine pilots can maneuver into hard-to-reach areas for insertions or retrievals, always a good person to have around on an aquatic adventure. This is mainly for smaller boats, not tanker-sized boats.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000091","name":"MARINER (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"mariner_L","tier":"L","months":144,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>While a common sailor may find himself at sea thanks to the blandishments and occasional force of the press-gang, the Mariner has chosen a life on the ocean wave. Years of hard training in the skills of seamanship and the arts of navigation transform youthful midshipmen into competent sailing masters, ship's mates and naval officers, who with luck, ability, favour and perhaps hard cash, will one day command their own ship.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000092","name":"MARTIAL ARTIST (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"martial_artist_L","tier":"L","months":73,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"Strength, Agility","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Strength, Agility"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>A martial artist is a warrior trained in the ways of unarmed combat and maneuvering. However, a martial artist is also schooled in the areas of knowledge and arts.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000093","name":"MARTIAL ARTS CHALLENGER (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"martial_arts_challenger_L","tier":"L","months":null,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"Strength","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Strength"},"qualifier":{"raw":"Any training package that gives Martial Arts attacks skill ranks. [-3 points]","type":"none","note":"Any training package that gives Martial Arts attacks skill ranks. [-3 points]"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The martial arts challenger is a character who lives and breathes in the martial arts world. He strives to prove himself the most skilled and powerful practitioner of his style of martial arts. By defeating all of the other martial artists in the area, he seeks to improve his reputation and the reputation of his chosen martial arts. Often the martial arts challenger seeks to build his reputation in order to open his own martial arts school.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000094","name":"MARTIAL ARTS CHAMPION (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"martial_arts_champion_V","tier":"V","months":null,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"None","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"None"},"qualifier":{"raw":"None","type":"none","note":"None"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The martial arts champion is a character who specializes in fighting for the causes of others. The he answers challenges posed to his family or employer. Not all martial arts champions fight for money, some are affiliated with a house or cause they serve by ties of blood or honor. Those martial arts champions that fight for money receive much less respect from their peers.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000095","name":"MARTIAL ARTS OPERA PERFORMER (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"martial_arts_opera_performer_L","tier":"L","months":null,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"Agility","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Agility"},"qualifier":{"raw":"None","type":"none","note":"None"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The martial arts opera performer is a character who has been trained at a very early age to participate in a type of acrobatic operacompany. The character has been trained to be flexible and acrobatic in order to accomplish the graceful but physically demanding traditional forms of the opera. To mimic the great warriors and heroes of the past, the performer has studied martial arts from a very young age. Most martial arts opera performers begin their apprenticeship at the age of six and continue in their profession the rest of their lives.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000096","name":"MARTIAL ARTS STREET PERFORMER (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"martial_arts_street_performer_V","tier":"V","months":null,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"None","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"None"},"qualifier":{"raw":"None","type":"none","note":"None"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The martial arts street performer is a character who uses his martial arts skills to gain money from spectators. He has a glib and agile tongue that often appears more skill ful than his martial arts skills. The martial arts street performer is also looked down upon by \"more serious\" (and wealthier) practitioners of the martial arts world. Yet one must cat, and it is honest work. Sometimes the performer is a martial artist who has fallen on hard times and is without patronage. Thus it can be very dangerous to bait inept street performers, as they may be skilled martial arts students new to their trade who will bitterly resent any slur on themselves and their newfound situation in life.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000097","name":"MEDIC (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"medic_V","tier":"V","months":51,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>Trained in the use of herbs, first aid, and the magic of his deity, the Medic has learned healing in many forms. He is often found in the temple, in a battle or on a mission to defend and watch over anyone that his religion asks to be protected and healed.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000098","name":"MEDIUM (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"medium_L","tier":"L","months":127,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"Intuition","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Intuition"},"qualifier":{"raw":"At list 10 ranks of skills in the Self Control skill category [-3 points]","type":"none","note":"At list 10 ranks of skills in the Self Control skill category [-3 points]"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>Medium works towards becoming a spiritual link between himself and his deity. He claims to know the will of his deity on many subjects. The medium is adept at all sorts of trances, and spends much time lost in his own world of meditation.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000099","name":"MERCENARY (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"mercenary_L","tier":"L","months":80,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":"1d10!open"},"statGains":{"raw":"Constitution","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Constitution"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>A mercenary is an independent soldier who works for the highest paying employer. Most armies have at least a few mercenaries to fill out their ranks (and some are comprised mostly of mercenaries). Most mercenaries are well-versed in more than one culture and have a good working knowledge of warfare.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000100","name":"MERCHANT (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"merchant_V","tier":"V","months":23,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":"1d10!open"},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>From the miserly old cloth-maker to the industrious, travelling silk merchant, everyone eventually deals with a seller of goods.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000101","name":"MILITARIA (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"militaria_L","tier":"L","months":150,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"A total of 7 ranks in any combination of the following skills: any skills in the Weapon group, any skills in the Martial Arts group, any skills in the Combat Maneuvers skill category, Tactics , Military Organization , Body Development . [-4 points]","type":"none","note":"A total of 7 ranks in any combination of the following skills: any skills in the Weapon group, any skills in the Martial Arts group, any skills in the Combat Maneuvers skill category, Tactics , Military Organization , Body Development . [-4 points]"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>This is the professional soldier. Be it Army, Navy, Army Air Corps, or Marines, the military life is well established within twentieth century society. Boot camp usually lasts the first three months; then it’s active duty thereafter. In the Militaria, one learns discipline and tactics. During wartime in the Pulp Era, most countries instituted some sort of “draft” to successfully fill out the ranks of their standing army or navy. It is the Militaria’s job to defend its nation’s boundaries, and sometimes to expand them. Famous members of the Militaria might include: Gen. Douglas MacArthur, George Patton, Dwight Eisenhower, Charles DeGualle, and Admiral Dewey.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000102","name":"MINISTER (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"minister_V","tier":"V","months":63,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"At list 10 ranks in Religion [-3 points]","type":"none","note":"At list 10 ranks in Religion [-3 points]"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>Ministers are responsible for the teaching within a religion. They are some of the most versed students of the doctrine and teachings of their religion that can be found. They spend their time sharing their thoughts with others of their own religion, and inviting all to attend their uplifting sermons.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000103","name":"MISSIONARY (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"missionary_L","tier":"L","months":149,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"Intuition","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Intuition"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The missionary is a peaceful emissary sent into far away lands to proselytize and convert. They travel a great deal, and teach many people in their journeys. While traveling, they encounter many different types of people and cultures. Many ignore the missionary, while others are searching for something that he might have to offer them.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000104","name":"MUSICIAN (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"musician_V","tier":"V","months":27,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>Musicians seek expression through the sound of music. A musician will usually know more than one instrument, although they will favor one above others.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000105","name":"NECROMANCER (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"necromancer_L","tier":"L","months":106,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"Intuition","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Intuition"},"qualifier":{"raw":"At least 7 ranks in Undead Lore and at least 4 ranks in the Necromancy spell list.","type":"none","note":"At least 7 ranks in Undead Lore and at least 4 ranks in the Necromancy spell list."},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>Digging up the past to work with the dead (hopefully to animate them), with plans of world domination are all part of day-to-day life for the Necromancer. His knowledge of the past allows him to find the remains of dead lords for the creation of the most powerful Undead.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000106","name":"NINJA (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"ninja_L","tier":"L","months":null,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"Agility, Constitution","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Agility, Constitution"},"qualifier":{"raw":"None","type":"none","note":"None"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The ninja is a character who has been raised by a secret clan of spies and assassins. Most of the character's life has been training for the jobs that he is going to do for his clan. In return for his training, the clan expects absolute loyalty — treachery is repaid in death for the offender. The clan teaches many types of skills including disguise, assassination, stealth, and endurance along with its weapon skills.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000107","name":"NOMENIST CASTER (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"nomenist_caster_L","tier":"L","months":42,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"None","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"None"},"qualifier":{"raw":"None","type":"none","note":"None"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The Nomenist is a master of language who forever seeks to learn new languages to find the words of the Primal Tongue that operate for themselves. Nomenists may be found in cosmopolitan cities or on the fringes of civilization in their pursuit of old or new languages.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000108","name":"OCCULTIST (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"occultist_L","tier":"L","months":null,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"Memory","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Memory"},"qualifier":{"raw":"A total of 5 ranks in any skills in the Lore group. If not playing in a No Magic campaign, a total of 2 ranks split between skills in the following skill categories: Power Awareness and Power Manipulation . [-4 points]","type":"none","note":"A total of 5 ranks in any skills in the Lore group. If not playing in a No Magic campaign, a total of 2 ranks split between skills in the following skill categories: Power Awareness and Power Manipulation . [-4 points]"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The Occultist is a scholar of the Paranormal. His greatest love is first and foremost the arts of the unknown; from research of magic and sorcery to investigations of mysterious phenomena, creatures and places. As an actual science, very few schools exist to educate the field. The real prerequisite for advancing in the vocation is an incurable thirst for knowledge, most often of “Things Man Was Not Meant To Know.” The information the Occultist seeks is always rare and cryptic, and he usually keeps a tight rein on any knowledge he has thus far acquired, for fear of allowing a competitor any advantage. Famous Occultists might include: Aleister Crowley, Edgar Cayce, Charles Fort, Professor J.B. Rhine, Charles Dexter Ward, Adolf Hitler, Dr. Rudolf Steiner.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000109","name":"ORACLE (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"oracle_L","tier":"L","months":83,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"Presence","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Presence"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>Trained in the divinatory arts and in history, the Oracle's impartial advice is sought by the great and the lowly from near and far to pierce the veil and reveal the future. Ambiguous prophecies, obtained by esoteric methods, must be interpreted by the querent, thus ensuring the Oracle's legendary accuracy.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000110","name":"PERFORMER (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"performer_V","tier":"V","months":40,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":"1d10!open"},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>A performer is a character who makes it his business to entertain crowds, large or small. He will often be found in taverns or perhaps in organized theaters. He is a restless soul, however, and will seldom stay in one place for very long.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000111","name":"PHILOSOPHER (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"philosopher_L","tier":"L","months":130,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"Reasoning","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Reasoning"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The Philosopher spends a great deal of time theorizing about the reasons things happen. He is not generally wellsuited for adventuring, but occasions do arise when his knowledge and/or wisdom is needed.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000112","name":"PHYSICIAN (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"physician_L","tier":"L","months":147,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":"1d10!open"},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>A professional healer, highly trained in the diagnosis and treatment of injury and illness, the Physician will normally be bound by vows and duties towards the patients. Competence is not without its price, and only the wealthy will easily afford the services of the Physician. Some Physicians may be employed on a permanent basis by noble families becoming trusted confidants, while others will set up independent medical practices in the cities.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000113","name":"PILGRIM (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"pilgrim_L","tier":"L","months":121,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"Memory","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Memory"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The pilgrim has lost his place of worship and is seeking another. His deity is still with him, but his church and religion have either been forcefully denied him or have been destroyed. He has had to wander the world looking for a place to freely practice his religion, perhaps being persecuted along the way. His life has become a search for his promised land.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000114","name":"POLITICAL (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"political_L","tier":"L","months":22,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>A pure social climber, the Politcal is totally amoral in his pursuit of power and prestige. The Political is kind only when it suits his needs. The Political’s theory is: “It is better to be feared than to be loved.” To this end he is ruthless and conniving, but he always tries to maintain a calculated dignified appearance.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000115","name":"POLITICIAN (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"politician_V","tier":"V","months":48,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>In the local or national arena, politicians operate in bureaucracies of governments. Socially adept and personable, they try to influence the government to their, and hopefully their constituents, viewpoint.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000116","name":"POTIONER (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"potioner_L","tier":"L","months":39,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"None","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"None"},"qualifier":{"raw":"A total of 6 ranks in Alchemy and Biochemistry [-3 points]","type":"none","note":"A total of 6 ranks in Alchemy and Biochemistry [-3 points]"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The potioner is a magical apothecary. The potioner uses spells to craft potions of healing, magic, and poison. The potioner may enhance normal herbs for general use as tonics and liniments or he may produce drugs that cloud the mind of the imbiber. Like an apothecary, the potioner attempts to draw the essence out ofnatural herbs to capture them in a bottle, but it is a rare potioner who manages by such sciences to create herbal remedies better than the simple animists of the wild.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000117","name":"PROPHET (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"prophet_L","tier":"L","months":98,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>A deity does not always go through standard channels in order to make his will known. When a deity chooses a spokesman from outside of the church it is generally because the church no longer listens to their deity as they should. People tend to scoff at prophets, thinking them mad. Clergy tend to frown on such unorthodox approaches to religion and may even persecute a prophet for heresy. A prophet finds little relief until his message gains acceptance or is proven true. For this reason, a deity only chooses followers of great faith and virtue for such a calling.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000118","name":"PROTECTOR (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"protector_L","tier":"L","months":95,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"Strength","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Strength"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>Protectors are holy warriors that are sent into the world by their church with the specific mission of protecting people from one specific sort of creature (Demons, Elementals, etc.). They will hunt this type of creature down with a fanatical zeal, and stop at nothing to see these creatures erased form the land.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000119","name":"PROTEGE (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"protege_L","tier":"L","months":105,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"realm stat","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"realm stat"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The sole or star pupil of a learned spell user, the Protege gains deep knowledge of a chosen area of magic, and a thorough understanding of the magical arts. Days spent in learning are repaid later with services rendered in assisting the mentor in his research and goals. Even if student surpasses master, or later rejects the ideals espoused by the mentor to follow another path, this long nurturing will shape and mold the Protege's world-view and lifestyle for the rest ofhis career.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000120","name":"ROMANTIC (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"romantic_L","tier":"L","months":74,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The art of seduction is a way of life to some individuals. A sweet phrase here, a gallant flourish there, the Romantic always makes the most of every situation. A Romantic may be overly competitive, overly optimistic, or just overly happy. In any event, the Romantic seeks to be the center of attention, especially with the opposite sex.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000121","name":"RUNEMASTER (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"runemaster_L","tier":"L","months":120,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"Memory, Empathy","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Memory, Empathy"},"qualifier":{"raw":"At least 4 ranks in the Rune Mastery spell list, and at least 5 ranks in the Read Runes skill, and at least 3 ranks in Symbol Lore , and a total of at least 25 ranks in written languaes..","type":"none","note":"At least 4 ranks in the Rune Mastery spell list, and at least 5 ranks in the Read Runes skill, and at least 3 ranks in Symbol Lore , and a total of at least 25 ranks in written languaes.."},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The intricacies of magical symbology intrigue the Runemaster, driving him to delve deeper into their secrets. He is seldom without a parchment nearby.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000122","name":"SAGE (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"sage_L","tier":"L","months":171,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"Memory","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Memory"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The Sage is the consummate scholar, with an unparalleled enthusiasm for learning, who acquires and assimilates knowledge from many sources, and can, by dint of special training, discern much from a simple examination of an object, whether it be commonplace or magical. Many Sages dedicate their lives to the preservation of knowledge, and will be found copying manuscripts in libraries or recording scraps of knowledge for posterity in their journals..</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000123","name":"SAILOR (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"sailor_V","tier":"V","months":28,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>A sailor rarely travels inland; preferring to feel the spray of the ocean on his face. He is perfectly at home on the water (though he might spend a bit of time in the taverns on the docks).</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000124","name":"SCHOOL MASTER (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"school_master_V","tier":"V","months":null,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"None","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"None"},"qualifier":{"raw":"None","type":"none","note":"None"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The school master is a character who has spent many years learning a specific martial arts style. Mis training involved long hours of practice and conditioning, but now the character is an acknowledged master of his given martial arts style.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000125","name":"SCIENTIST (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"scientist_L","tier":"L","months":141,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"Memory and Reasoning","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Memory and Reasoning"},"qualifier":{"raw":"At least 1 skill in the Science/Analytic group at 2 ranks. [-4 points]","type":"none","note":"At least 1 skill in the Science/Analytic group at 2 ranks. [-4 points]"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>White lab coats, mazes of glass tubing connecting beakers of bubbling, colored liquids and sparking electrodes were the typical perceptions of the scientist in the 1930s. While real scientists rarely had labs that resembled Dr. Frankenstein’s, they were making significant gains in the various sciences without them. Technology was growing quickly and its effect on the general public was profound. Devices like the telephone, aerosol cans, radio, pressurized airplanes and other inventions changed the world. Famous names in the scientific ranks include: Albert Einstein, Hans Zarkov, Enrico Fermi, Clark Savage, Jr. , Andrew Blodgett Mayfair, Thomas J. Roberts, William Harper Littlejohn, and Thomas Edison.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000126","name":"SCOUT (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"scout_V","tier":"V","months":33,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":"1d10!open"},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>Scouts can find employment in a variety of settings. Their general duties include travelling in front of a group for the purposes of finding hazards and/or dangers for the rest of the group to avoid.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000127","name":"SECRET SOCIETY MEMBER (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"secret_society_member_V","tier":"V","months":null,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"None","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"None"},"qualifier":{"raw":"None","type":"none","note":"None"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The secret society member is a character who has been pulled from other walks of life and introduced to a secret movement. The current government does not support the movement's goals and thus the movement must keep a low profile. Members are taught how to fight and defend themselves for the time when the movement will come out of hiding and accomplish its goals.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000128","name":"SERVITOR (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"servitor_V","tier":"V","months":41,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>Servitors are lower class nobles or higher class commoners who serve in a lord’s castle. A servitor could be anything from a page to a lady-in-waiting. Servitors receive very little compensation for their duties, but they gain great respect out of their close familiarity with the ruling class. In many ways the job of the Servitor can be boiled down to being paid to provide companionship. For this reason they are especially adept at being sociable and agreeable, because they have few other skills.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000129","name":"SHAMAN PRIEST (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"shaman_priest_L","tier":"L","months":69,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"Intuition, Presence","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Intuition, Presence"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>In tribal communities, there are seldom organized churches. Instead, the groups often lead by a single religious leader. This leader will often use animal totems and other forces of nature to assist him in his duties.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000130","name":"SIEGE ENGINEER (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"siege_engineer_V","tier":"V","months":29,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The Siege Engineer specializes in the destruction and reduction of castle defenses. Siege Engineers can organize military operations relating to sapping castle walls, building siege engines, and employing siege engines.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000131","name":"SOLDIER (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"soldier_V","tier":"V","months":26,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":"1d10!open"},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>In almost every culture there is a professional warrior; whose job is to protect the peoples of that culture. If a promotion is gained (in the Special section), the character has been promoted in the ranks (more promotions equate to higher ranks).</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000132","name":"SPECIAL FORCES OPERATIVE (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"special_forces_operative_L","tier":"L","months":116,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"choice of Constitution or Strength","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"choice of Constitution or Strength"},"qualifier":{"raw":"A total of 15 ranks in skills from the following groups: Athletic, Awareness, Subterfuge, and/or Weapon.","type":"none","note":"A total of 15 ranks in skills from the following groups: Athletic, Awareness, Subterfuge, and/or Weapon."},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>This package represents persons who plan, organize, operate and carry-out high-risk black ops for the military. This class is dedicated, loyal, and will follow their orders, sometimes to their own demise.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000133","name":"SPELL RESEARCHER (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"spell_researcher_V","tier":"V","months":114,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"None","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"None"},"qualifier":{"raw":"A total of 20 ranks in skills in the Lore group [-5 points]","type":"none","note":"A total of 20 ranks in skills in the Lore group [-5 points]"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>A spell researcher is constantly drawn to the boundaries of known magic. The researcher seeks to understand why magic works, and looks for new ways to make it work. Whether he studies the varying theories of the realms of magic or its more practical applications, the researcher seeks to add to the growing stores of magical knowledge, often without regard to the effect their findings may have on the world around them.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000134","name":"SPELL STUDENT (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"spell_student_V","tier":"V","months":105,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"None","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"None"},"qualifier":{"raw":"Total temporary stats for Memory and Reasoning of 180 or greater [-5 points]","type":"none","note":"Total temporary stats for Memory and Reasoning of 180 or greater [-5 points]"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>A spell student is taught the lessons of magic by a collegium or school of magic. Students learn magic from a number of different masters in classroom settings as well as independently in the college's library. Students have exposure to a tremendous variety of spell lists and magic theories, which often makes them the most educated of spell casters. Of course, students also tend to lack practical \"real world\" experience, having spent so much time cloistered in their studies. Students may either learn spells to assist them in city life or less often spells to assist in practicing abroad.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000135","name":"SPY (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"spy_V","tier":"V","months":44,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":"1d10!open"},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>A spy is a person who makes it his job to infiltrate enemy positions, gather information, and return that information to his people.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000136","name":"STUDENT (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"student_V","tier":"V","months":41,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>This package attempts to simulate higher education; B.A. , M.S. , etc. These degree levels are for academic or science skills, but not for more intense science/vocational skills, i.e. medical or engineering degrees. This is for a person who wants the educational experience of college.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000137","name":"TEMPLAR (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"templar_L","tier":"L","months":94,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"Strength","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Strength"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The Templars are holy warriors that defend temples and other holy ground. Often without any magic of their own, they nevertheless will give their lives for the cause. At a moment's notice, they are willing to drop everything and join a crusade for the faith.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000138","name":"TEMPLE MONK (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"temple_monk_V","tier":"V","months":null,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"Self Discipline","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Self Discipline"},"qualifier":{"raw":"None","type":"none","note":"None"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The temple monk is a character who has spent most of his life in the sheltered walls of a temple learning both his religious doctrines and his martial arts skills. The temple monk is often surprised by the corruption in the material world, but he is not defenseless thanks to his extensive training. A temple monk strives to renounce the material world and pursue only his spiritual development.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000139","name":"TERRORIST (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"terrorist_V","tier":"V","months":27,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":"1d10!open"},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>Terrorists use coercion to promote a belief system or a set of goals. This usually translates into the use of violence, or the threat of violence, to advance their cause, but not always. The destruction of property combined with vandalism, usually found with animal rights activists, is another form of terrorism on the rise.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000140","name":"THEOLOGIAN (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"theologian_L","tier":"L","months":100,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"Presence and Memory","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Presence and Memory"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>A Theologian has a particular belief, but usually knows something about some other religion’s beliefs. This could be anyone from the Catholic priest taking confession to the Jewish Rabbi counseling his followers. Theologians sometimes are instructors in universities throughout the world, such as the Catholic Society of Jesuits.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000141","name":"THEURGIST (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"theurgist_L","tier":"L","months":116,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"Constitution and Intuition","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Constitution and Intuition"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>A Theurgist is the battlefield medic of religious troops. They normally travel with the regular troops and are sometimes even part of them. Many standing religious armies have at least two or three of these \"miracle workers\" within their ranks, sometimes with as many as one per unit. They are the fighting healers, using their talents out on the battlefield to help those who would otherwise not survive the trip to the infirmary.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000142","name":"TRAVELLER (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"traveller_V","tier":"V","months":18,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The traveller is simply that, a traveller. He is somewhat knowledgeable about his local region and knows the basics of the outdoors.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000143","name":"TROUBADOUR (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"troubadour_L","tier":"L","months":132,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The Troubadour is a wandering minstrel who brings tales of wonder, gossip, and news to otherwise isolated towns, farmsteads, and castles. The Troubadour can expect good food and shelter if he tells a good tale even in the humblest of homes. A Troubadour is more than just a performer. The Troubadour is a professional traveller, entertainer, and gossip. The Troubadour lives his life in search of excitement, adventure, and a warm crowd to whom he can relate his tales.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000144","name":"UNDERCOVER AGENT (V)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"undercover_agent_V","tier":"V","months":59,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>Undercover Agents have a very dangerous job; they must cover their identity with either someone else’s or a fictitious one without ever forgetting that they are a law enforcement officer. There is only one rule when going under: never, ever blow your cover. This takes a lot of self-control and even more insane courage.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000145","name":"VIZIER (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"vizier_L","tier":"L","months":113,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":"1d10!open"},"statGains":{"raw":"none","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"none"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>Viziers serve royal patrons as advisors on affairs of state and magic. A Vizier divines the future, investigates magical affairs, and generally advises his lord in affairs of state. In return, a Vizier expects good pay, status, and the luxury of private research. Viziers often find it difficult not to abuse their dual status as magician and advisor. Of course, as long as the lord is satisfied, who will speak against them?</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000146","name":"WANDERER (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"wanderer_L","tier":"L","months":95,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"Constitution","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Constitution"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The wanderer is similar to a traveller, except he has no “home” region. He has forsaken any roots and chooses instead to wander the world.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000147","name":"WANDERING MONK (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"wandering_monk_L","tier":"L","months":null,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"None","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"None"},"qualifier":{"raw":"None","type":"none","note":"None"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The wandering monk is a character who has spent some time in training at the temples of the region, but later decided that true wisdom is to be found by interacting with the people. In the course of his travels, the wandering monk learns the need for a strong defense and gains a better understanding of human nature.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000148","name":"WARLOCK (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"warlock_L","tier":"L","months":76,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"Empathy","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Empathy"},"qualifier":{"raw":"At least 4 ranks in any Spell Mastery skills and at least 3 ranks in any one Direct Spells skill.","type":"none","note":"At least 4 ranks in any Spell Mastery skills and at least 3 ranks in any one Direct Spells skill."},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>Where subtle machinations would fail, the overt power of magic will prevail. The Warlock seeks to control those around him with magic.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000149","name":"WARRIOR-PRIEST (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"warrior_priest_L","tier":"L","months":null,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"None","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"None"},"qualifier":{"raw":"None","type":"none","note":"None"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>The warrior-priest is a character who has studied at a militant temple to serve in the enforcement arm of the temple. The warrior-priest believes that he has been called to defend his religion and the goals it professes.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000150","name":"WEAPON MASTER (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"weapon_master_L","tier":"L","months":95,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"Strength, Agility","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Strength, Agility"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>A weapon master has made a life out of studying and perfecting the use of weapons. However, he seldom has learned much beyond the use of weapons.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000151","name":"WITCH (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"witch_L","tier":"L","months":162,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"Empathy","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Empathy"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>A Witch is a Channeler that usually stays away from civilized society as a recluse that only leaves his or her home with definite goals in mind. A Witch often has a Demon as his Channeling source of power. Witches are in contact with Demons or other supernatural creatures often, for their own hidden and questionable purposes.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
{"_id":"eqtp000000000152","name":"ZEALOT (L)","type":"training_package","img":"systems/eqrmss/assets/Icons/game/abstract-050.svg","system":{"rmssKey":"zealot_L","tier":"L","months":73,"startingMoney":{"base":"normal","roll":null},"statGains":{"raw":"Intuition","count":null,"mode":null,"stats":[],"note":"Intuition"},"qualifier":{"raw":"none","type":"none","note":"none"},"lifestyleSkills":[],"description":"<p>A zealot is a fanatic for a religion. They are generally enthusiastic, but not necessarily aggressive.</p>"},"effects":[],"flags":{},"folder":null}
